<title>HUNGARY: Hungary six-month bill yield falls to 22.40.</title>
<headline>Hungary six-month bill yield falls to 22.40.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average annual yield on the latest issue of six-month discount treasury bills was set by auction at 22.40 percent, down from 22.59 percent at an auction two weeks ago, the Government Debt Management Agency said.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow, and on  HTBO.</p>
<p>    Total on offer	    12,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total bids received     29,837.50 million forints</p>
<p>    Total allocated	   12,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total issued		13,500 million forints</p>
<p>    Average annual yield	    22.40 pct</p>
<p>    Average price		     90.0026 pct</p>
</text>
